#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:5
#: f714766dd2814d8e882a92ef4c8fbc0b
msgid "Flip Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:7
#: 41b449f8be8841edb202ce84ae0843e3
msgid "Vehicle will flip on its roll or pitch axis depending upon the pilot's roll and pitch stick position in flight mode's which allow this (ACRO/ALTHOLD/STABILIZE...and,of course, FLIP mode). Vehicle will increase throttle rapidly as it starts to flip. Once the flip is completed, canceled, or times out, the original flight mode the vehicle was in will be restored. The flip will end at the entry attitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:9
#: 691669fcc6f74fe7946282aa70c3e41b
msgid "The vehicle will not flip again until the switch is brought low and back to high, if on an :ref:`Auxiliary Switch <common-auxiliary-functions>`, or if the mode channel switch is changed to another mode and back to FLIP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:11
#: 5b3f96e191e74594a04fe5c3d318596a
msgid "Give yourself at least 10m of altitude before trying flip for the first time!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:14
#: 8f4638d6bfdf49368cb9d5f83e67c721
msgid "Flip Mode Controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:15
#: ab8f0fcb744b49468aaa61c0a4896eec
msgid "The mode may be entered either by an :ref:`Auxiliary Switch <common-auxiliary-functions>`, or by changing flight mode to FLIP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:17
#: 3d41f9d4fe4f4da0b674d9c971c37b52
msgid "The direction of the flip defaults to ROLL LEFT, but if the RC Pitch stick is moved slightly back or forward, it will flip on the pitch axis, back or forward, respectively. If the RC Pitch stick is neutral but the RC ROLL is pushed slightly right, it will flip rolling to the right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:18
#: 4352f082db554b7b8ce65c65c38880ab
msgid "During the flip the throttle is managed to attempt to neither gain or lose altitude. It is only an attempt!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:19
#: 9ce6491bf663484c820efd1ab921b5ba
msgid "You may abort the flip by moving the pitch or roll stick as if to command near full stick in that axis. The Flip will immediately halt **at whatever attitude it is currently at** and return to the previous flight mode at the pilot's throttle stick input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flip-mode.rst:20
#: e5de562d057745359daab7d518def705
msgid "As the flip is completing, it will briefly increase throttle to try to recover any lost altitude. Again, this is an approximation. Once completed (entry attitude re-attained), the previous flight mode is returned to (if not entered by an AUX switch). It will not flip again until the Aux Switch is lowered and raised again, if used, or FLIP flight mode re-entered. If entered via a flight mode switch, you will need to change mode out of FLIP, to another mode, and then back again if another flip is desired,"
msgstr ""
